<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 1: </span><span id="S2.T1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Result</span>: DeepCache leads to a surge in memory usage, while FME decreases the speed-up, and both may cause quality degradation across different models. In contrast, our approach not only preserves quality but also accelerates inference and reduces memory consumption to below the baseline model. N means that the feature map is recalculated once every N steps. </figcaption>
</figure>
